arse-blockades-yield-a-nice-blockade"]},{"convention":"A regular expression is a formal syntax tree, while its denotation is a language; the constructors +, concatenation, and star act syntactically and are interpreted recursively.","fixed_by":"def-regular-expression-syntax","matters_for":["def-regular-expression-denotation","thm-regular-expression-to-epsilon-nfa","thm-dfa-to-regular-expression","thm-kleenes-theorem","fs-regular-expression-syntax-is-its-denoted-language"]},{"convention":"The CFL pumping parameter p is chosen before the word, while Ogden's p is chosen before both the word and its marked positions; admissibility requires a marked position in vx and at most p marked positions in vwx.","fixed_by":"thm-pumping-lemma-for-context-free-languages","matters_for":["thm-ogdens-lemma","thm-cfls-are-not-closed-under-intersection","ex-pumping-lemma-for-context-free-languages","fs-the-cfl-pumping-lemma-characterizes-cfls"]},{"convention":"CYK uses CNF binary and terminal productions for nonempty inputs; epsilon is handled separately by the exceptional start production.","fixed_by":"def-cyk-table-and-span-variable","matters_for":["lem-cyk-table-invariant","thm-cyk-membership-algorithm","cor-cfl-membership-is-decidable","fs-cyk-needs-no-normal-form-preprocessing"]},{"convention":"The fixed machine code uses right-infinite tapes, encodes L by 0 and R by 1, and clamps an L-move at head position 0.","fixed_by":"def-effective-encoding-of-turing-machines","matters_for":["lem-machine-encoding-is-injective-and-decodable","thm-stay-put-moves-can-be-eliminated","lem-step-by-step-interpreter-for-machine-codes","thm-existence-of-a-universal-turing-machine","ex-effective-enumeration-of-turing-machines"]}],"load_bearing":[{"id":"thm-the-star-expansion-four-family-of-a-forest-has-the-erdos-hajnal-property","statement":"For every forest F, the family {F^star, (overline F)^star, overline{F^star}, overline{(overline F)^star}} has the Erd\u0005os-Hajnal property.","used_by":["cor-the-star-expansion-of-the-four-vertex-path-and-its-complement-have-the-erdos-hajnal-property","thm-a-forest-complement-and-its-star-expansion-have-the-erdos-hajnal-property"]},{"id":"thm-co-p-five-free-graphs-admit-a-pure-or-x-sparse-polynomial-blockade","statement":"There exists d>=40 such that every sufficiently large overline{P_5}-free graph has a pure or x-sparse polynomial-width blockade of some length k in [2,x^{-1}].","used_by":["thm-the-five-vertex-path-is-nice","lem-refining-the-largest-layout-block-forces-local-blockade-length-at-least-epsilon-inverse","thm-local-pure-or-x-sparse-blockades-yield-a-nice-blockade"]},{"id":"thm-the-five-vertex-path-has-the-polynomial-rodl-property","statement":"The graph P_5 has the polynomial R\u0005odl property.","used_by":["cor-the-five-vertex-path-and-its-complement-have-the-erdos-hajnal-property"]},{"id":"thm-kleenes-theorem","statement":"Let L subseteq Sigma^*. Then L is regular if and only if there exists a regular expression R over Sigma with L(R)=L.","used_by":["thm-closure-under-homomorphic-image"]},{"id":"thm-pumping-lemma-for-context-free-languages","statement":"Every context-free language has a pumping length p such that each word z of length at least p admits z=uvwxy with |vx|>=1, |vwx|<=p, and uv^iwx^iy in L for every i>=0.","used_by":["thm-cfls-are-not-closed-under-intersection","ex-pumping-lemma-for-context-free-languages","fs-the-cfl-pumping-lemma-characterizes-cfls"]},{"id":"thm-cyk-membership-algorithm","statement":"For a CNF grammar, CYK accepts epsilon exactly for S->epsilon and a nonempty word w exactly when S lies in the top CYK cell; it decides membership in L(G).","used_by":["cor-cfl-membership-is-decidable","fs-cyk-needs-no-normal-form-preprocessing"]},{"id":"lem-step-by-step-interpreter-for-machine-codes","statement":"A fixed deterministic one-tape machine maps a valid coded configuration to its unique one-step successor code, returns a halting configuration code unchanged, and returns a fixed malformed output on malformed input.","used_by":["thm-existence-of-a-universal-turing-machine"]}],"published_dependencies":[{"id":"lem-finite-tuples-admit-effective-prefix-free-encodings","used_for":"Fixing and decoding the tuple format used by the machine-code construction.","opened":true},{"id":"def-effective-binary-encoding-and-decoder","used_for":"The meaning of an effective prefix-free encoding and total malformed-code decoder.","opened":true},{"id":"def-parse-tree-and-yield","used_for":"CNF height/yield bounds and the parse-tree pumping arguments.","opened":true},{"id":"def-chomsky-normal-form","used_for":"The allowed binary, terminal, and exceptional epsilon productions behind pumping and CYK.","opened":true},{"id":"thm-chomsky-normal-form","used_for":"Replacing an arbitrary CFG by an equivalent CNF grammar.","opened":true},{"id":"thm-derivation-parse-tree-correspondence","used_for":"Passing between CFG membership/derivations and parse trees.","opened":true},{"id":"def-turing-machine-configuration","used_for":"The canonical finite configuration representation used by the one-step interpreter.","opened":true},{"id":"def-one-step-configuration-relation","used_for":"The clamped left-boundary successor rule implemented by the interpreter.","opened":true},{"id":"def-halting-computation-and-divergence","used_for":"The halting and divergence semantics used by universality and its counterexample.","opened":true}],"concerns":[{"id":"lem-a-sparse-p-five-free-graph-has-an-anticomplete-two-blockade","concern":"Step 2.1 does not follow: C\\N[v] can have many connected components, so a largest component need not have size at least eta|V(G)|; the later B has no established size lower bound either. The cited primary source's Lemma 4.4 obtains a component of size at least |G|/2 under the assumed failure of the desired blockade and then performs two further component arguments, none of which appears here.","severity":"would-be-fatal"},{"id":"thm-pumping-lemma-for-context-free-languages","concern":"Step 2.1 bounds the upper A-subtree by counting only the selected root-to-leaf path. That does not bound another, deeper branch of that subtree unless the selected path was chosen globally longest; the proof never makes that choice. Choosing a longest path repairs the standard argument.","severity":"gap-a-reader-closes"},{"id":"thm-ogdens-lemma","concern":"Step 3.1's branch-point count has an off-by-one/error in its claimed bound: more than 2^{|V|} marked leaves does not force more than |V| branch points below the selected upper node. The needed p-admissibility bound can be recovered by using the stated p=2^{|V|+1} threshold, but the displayed inference is not valid as written.","severity":"gap-a-reader-closes"},{"id":"thm-existence-of-a-universal-turing-machine","concern":"Step 2.1 says the one-step interpreter returns the same configuration code unchanged exactly in the halting case. A nonhalting configuration can also be its own successor, for example a left move at head position 0 that writes the same symbol and preserves the state. The subsequent explicit accepting/rejecting-state check is sufficient, so deleting the 'exactly' assertion repairs the proof.","severity":"gap-a-reader-closes"}],"alerts":[],"seams_checked":[]}